Note: clicking the sound button toggled soundOn to false (startAudio() + setSound(!true) = setSound(false)) — so the audio context is running but master gain is 0. Hmm — the first click on the sound button is both a gesture and a toggle. This is a UX bug: a user who clicks "sound on" first (to give the gesture) will end up muting it. Let me fix wireUI: on the first click (if audio hasn't started yet), start the audio and keep the current preference (don't toggle). Only toggle on subsequent clicks:

